<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 346.6 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 346.6 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of January 9 raised 346.6 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 307.5 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 107.85 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.24 (14.27)	   40.6 (37.7)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.08 (16.13)	   49.4 (53.9)</p>
<p>    12 months		 16.90 (16.90)	   62.5 (55.0)</p>
<p>    24 months		 19.02 (19.28)	  194.1 (160.9)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,551.25 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,551.75 a week earlier and 1,594 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
